timeline
    title AI History — From Turing to Transformers (1936–2025)
    section Foundations of Computing (1936–1955)
        1936 : Universal Turing Machine : Turing — basis of all computation
        1950 : The Turing Test : "Can machines think?" — imitation game
        1955 : AI term coined : John McCarthy — Dartmouth proposal
    section Birth of AI (1956–1969)
        1956 : Dartmouth Conference : AI becomes an official field
        1957 : Perceptron : Rosenblatt — first trainable neural model
        1966 : ELIZA : Weizenbaum, MIT — first conversational chatbot
    section First AI Winter (1970–1979)
        1973 : Lighthill Report : UK slashes AI funding — over-promised, under-delivered
        1974 : Back-propagation : Werbos PhD — ignored for a decade
    section Expert Systems Era (1980–1987)
        1980 : XCON/R1 : First commercial expert system at DEC — saves $40M/year
        1982 : Hopfield Networks : Neural networks revived — wins 2024 Nobel Prize
        1986 : Back-prop published : Rumelhart, Hinton, Williams — Nature paper
    section Second AI Winter (1987–1993)
        1988 : Bayesian Networks : Judea Pearl — probabilistic reasoning under uncertainty
        1989 : LeNet CNN : Yann LeCun, Bell Labs — reads zip codes for US postal service
    section Statistical AI Rise (1994–2005)
        1997 : Deep Blue : IBM defeats Kasparov — first public AI triumph
        1997 : LSTM : Hochreiter & Schmidhuber — solves the vanishing gradient problem
        2005 : DARPA Grand Challenge : Stanford's Stanley drives 132 miles autonomously
    section Deep Learning Renaissance (2006–2011)
        2006 : Deep Belief Networks : Geoffrey Hinton — coins "Deep Learning"
        2007 : NVIDIA CUDA : GPU unlocks massive parallelism for AI training
        2011 : IBM Watson : Wins Jeopardy! — NLP at human expert level
    section Modern Deep Learning (2012–2016)
        2012 : AlexNet : Wins ImageNet by a landslide — deep learning revolution ignites
        2014 : GANs : Ian Goodfellow — generative AI is born
        2016 : AlphaGo : Defeats Lee Sedol 4-1 — Go mastered, AI Sputnik moment
    section Transformer Era (2017–2025)
        2017 : Transformer : "Attention Is All You Need" — foundation of all modern LLMs
        2022 : ChatGPT : 100M users in 2 months — mainstream AI revolution via RLHF
        2024 : OpenAI o1 : Chain-of-thought reasoning — AI that thinks before answering
